# =============================================================================
# Jamee — environment variables
# =============================================================================
#
# Requirement 17.2: every required variable name, a placeholder value, NO real secret.
# Requirement 13.7: only NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed values may reach the browser.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in. `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` says where each value
# comes from, step by step. `.env.example` itself is COMMITTED — it must never hold a live
# credential, a real connection string, or a real token.
#
# HOW FAILURE LOOKS. Every variable below is read through `serverEnv()` in `src/lib/env.ts`,
# which validates on FIRST USE and throws naming the missing variable. There is no silent
# default and no `process.env.X!` anywhere else in the codebase — an absent variable fails the
# request that needed it, loudly, rather than producing a wrong answer for a farmer.
#
# AMENDMENT A3 — MongoDB replaces Supabase. There is no Supabase URL, no anon/publishable key,
# and no service-role key anymore: the browser opens no database connection and holds no
# database credential. The only database credential is the server-only MONGODB_URI, held solely
# by `src/lib/db/client.ts`. Google sign-in runs through the in-app auth library (Better Auth,
# V35), whose secret and Google client id/secret are Jamee's own server-only variables.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. Model identifiers, header names, and platform limits are
# compile-time constants in `src/lib/config/verified.ts`, and the recharge price, the recharge
# period, and the link-token TTL are compile-time constants in `src/lib/config/access.ts` —
# each read from exactly one place and from no environment variable (criteria 21.4, 22.4). A
# price in an env var is an unversioned, unreviewable change to what Jamee charges.
#
# There is also no JAMEE_TEST_DATABASE_URL: under A3 the integration tests run against an
# in-process `mongodb-memory-server` replica set (V31), not an external test database.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The complete set, at a glance
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The authority for this list is `serverEnvSchema` / `PUBLIC_ENV_VARS` / `OPTIONAL_SERVER_ENV_KEYS`
# in `src/lib/env.ts` and `src/lib/env.public.ts` — not this comment. `ALL_ENV_KEYS` is exported
# from `env.ts` so a completeness check (Property 30) compares against the schema, not prose.
#
#   PUBLIC (reach the browser, by design)
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME       REQUIRED — the <bot> in the link deep link (V24)
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID             REQUIRED — the public key id the checkout uses (V27)
#
#   SERVER ONLY — secrets and connection string
#     MONGODB_URI                             REQUIRED (V28, V32) — includes the database name
#     BETTER_AUTH_SECRET                      REQUIRED (V30, V35)
#     BETTER_AUTH_URL                         REQUIRED (V30)
#     GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID                        REQUIRED (V30)
#     GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET                    REQUIRED (V30)
#     GEMINI_API_KEY                          REQUIRED
#     GROQ_API_KEY                            REQUIRED
#     TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN                      REQUIRED (V24)
#     TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET_TOKEN           REQUIRED (V24, D12)
#     RAZORPAY_KEY_ID                         REQUIRED (V27) — same value as the public name above
#     RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET                     REQUIRED (V27)
#     RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET                 REQUIRED (V27, D15)
#     CRON_SECRET                             REQUIRED (min 16 chars, V21)
#
# "REQUIRED" above means exactly what the Zod schema says: `serverEnv('NAME')` throws when the
# value is missing or empty. The compile-time constants — the recharge price and period, the
# link-token TTL, model identifiers, header names, platform limits — are NOT here.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public (these DO reach the browser, by design)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. The Telegram bot username, WITHOUT the leading @ — the `<bot>` in the
# `https://t.me/<bot>?start=<token>` link deep link the web profile screen builds (V24,
# Requirement 21.6). NOT a secret: it is in the link every farmer opens.
# Where: the username you gave @BotFather when you created the bot.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=your_bot_username

# REQUIRED. The Razorpay key id the browser checkout initializes with (V27). This is the SAME
# value as the server RAZORPAY_KEY_ID below; it is duplicated under a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name so the
# unprefixed one is never read from a client component. It is a public identifier, not a secret —
# the key SECRET, which signs orders, is server-only.
# Where: Razorpay dashboard → Settings → API Keys. Test-mode ids start `rzp_test_`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_0000000000000000


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MongoDB — server only
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. MongoDB Atlas connection string — the ONLY database credential (V28, V32). Held
# solely by `src/lib/db/client.ts`, which begins with `import 'server-only'` and caches one
# MongoClient on globalThis within the M0 500-connection limit. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# Where: MongoDB Atlas → your M0 cluster → Connect → Drivers → copy the "mongodb+srv://…" URI.
# The URI MUST include the database name `jamee` in the path (…mongodb.net/jamee?…), otherwise
# the driver connects with no default database and every collection access fails.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://your-user:your-password@your-cluster.mongodb.net/jamee?retryWrites=true&w=majority


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Better Auth + Google sign-in — server only
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Better Auth session signing/encryption secret (V30, V35). The library reads this
# exact name. Read only by `src/lib/auth/*`. Use a long random string.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-better-auth-secret

# REQUIRED. Better Auth base URL (V30) — the deployed origin, e.g. https://jamee.example.com,
# or http://localhost:3000 for local development. Used to build the Google OAuth callback; an
# absent value lets the callback default to localhost, which breaks a deployed sign-in.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# REQUIRED. Google OAuth client id (V30). Read only by `src/lib/auth/*`.
# Where: Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client ID.
# Register the redirect URI http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google (dev) and
# https://<domain>/api/auth/callback/google (prod).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# REQUIRED. Google OAuth client secret (V30). Server-only, never public.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-your-google-oauth-client-secret


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI providers — server only
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Google Gemini. Primary for `vision-classify` and `text-generate`.
# Where: Google AI Studio → Get API key.
#
# V6 records that the `@google/genai` client reads this exact name itself. `src/lib/gemini.ts`
# still passes it through `serverEnv()` so a missing key fails with env.ts's message rather than
# the SDK's. The model identifier is pinned in `src/lib/config/verified.ts` (V6), not here.
GEMINI_API_KEY=replace-with-your-gemini-api-key

# REQUIRED. Groq. Text fallback (V8), conditional vision fallback (V9), and transcription (V10).
# Where: Groq Console → API Keys. Real keys start `gsk_`.
#
# One key serves all three; a Groq outage therefore takes voice offline while image and chat
# continue on Gemini. That is a known single point of failure, not a defect.
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_replace_with_your_groq_api_key

# NOTE — there is no VISION_FALLBACK_MODEL variable, and that is deliberate.
# The vision fallback is the compile-time constant `VISION_FALLBACK_MODEL` in
# `src/lib/config/verified.ts`, typed `string | null`. V9 records that Groq's vision models are
# *Preview* tier — "may be discontinued at short notice" — so setting that constant to `null`
# has to stay expressible: the gateway then returns a one-member chain and Requirement 14.8's
# single exhausted-chain branch keeps the farmer-visible behaviour identical. Nothing to set here.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram Bot API — server only
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. The bot token @BotFather issued (V24). Every outbound call — setWebhook,
# sendMessage, and the getFile download URL — is built from it.
# Where: Telegram → @BotFather → your bot → API Token. A real token looks like
# `123456789:AA...` — a numeric bot id, a colon, then a secret.
# Read only by `src/lib/telegram.ts`.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456789:replace-with-your-telegram-bot-token

# REQUIRED. The secret string Jamee registers through setWebhook, which Telegram then presents
# in the X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token header of every delivery (V24, D12). The webhook route
# compares this in constant time BEFORE parsing the body; an absent value is a FAILED
# verification (401), not a skipped one. You invent it; V24 allows 1–256 chars of
# A-Z a-z 0-9 _ and -. Use a long random string.
TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET_TOKEN=invent-a-long-random-webhook-secret-token


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Razorpay — server only  (public key id is NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, above)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Razorpay key id (V27). The SAME value as NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID above — set
# both to the same id. This unprefixed name is read server-side (order creation) and never from
# a client component; the duplication is what keeps that true.
# Where: Razorpay dashboard → Settings → API Keys. Test-mode ids start `rzp_test_`.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_0000000000000000

# REQUIRED. Razorpay key SECRET (V27). Signs order creation. Server-only, never public.
# Where: Razorpay dashboard → Settings → API Keys — shown ONCE when you generate the key pair.
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=replace-with-your-razorpay-key-secret

# REQUIRED. Razorpay webhook secret (V27, D15). HMAC-SHA256 key for the X-Razorpay-Signature
# over the RAW request body, verified before any JSON parsing. An absent value is a FAILED
# verification (401), not a skipped one — a deployment that forgot this must not become one
# where anyone can grant an entitlement by POSTing a body.
# Where: Razorpay dashboard → Settings → Webhooks → the secret you set when adding the webhook.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=invent-a-long-random-webhook-secret


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retention sweep — server only
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Requirement 18.12's retention sweep secret. Minimum 16 characters, enforced by the
# schema; use a password generator.
# Where: you invent it, then set it as a project environment variable on the deployment
# platform (and in `.env.local` for a local manual run).
#
# Named CRON_SECRET because that is the name the platform injects: V21 records that Vercel
# automatically sends this variable's value as `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` on every
# cron invocation, so a differently named variable could not be used for automatic triggering
# at all. There is one secret here, not two.
#
# /api/internal/retention-sweep reads ONLY this header. A valid farmer session is explicitly
# not authorization for that route (Requirement 18.13).
CRON_SECRET=generate-a-random-string-of-at-least-16-characters
